<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5724" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Brŏtĕas</span></b> , ae,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βροτέας</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>One of the Lapithœ</i>, <i>slain by the Centaur Gryneus at the marriage festival of
				Perseus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12,
			262</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Twin-brother of Ammon</i>, <i>and with
				him slain by Phineus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5,
				107</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A son of Vulcan and Minerva</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
			515</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
